    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (42 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional `postcode` field on owner creation, validated only when present.\n\n**What the rule does:** A 4-digit `postcode` supplied on `POST /api/owners` must be valid for the owner's city per the fixed region table (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000-2099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000-3099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000-4099). A city with no known region accepts any 4-digit postcode. Out-of-range or malformed postcodes are rejected with **400**; an absent postcode is accepted (backward-compatible), and a supplied postcode is stored and returned.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the optional `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated DTOs carry it on both the create request and the `Owner` response.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `postcode` column, getter, and setter (MapStruct maps it by name in both directions automatically).\n- **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a `postcode` column to the `owners` table.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a `validatePostcode(city, postcode)` step (alongside the existing telephone/email/address normalization). It returns `null` when absent/blank, rejects non-4-digit values, and enforces the region range via a fixed `REGION_POSTCODE_RANGES` table, reusing the existing `Localities.region(city)` lookup.\n- **`InvalidPostcodeException`** + a handler in **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 maps the failure to a 400 with the same `ProblemDetail` shape as the other field validators.\n\nThe new `Cp29Tests` (valid stored/returned, absent accepted, malformed rejected) and the postcode-dependent `Cp13Tests` pass, along with all 42 tests.",
